{"tool_name":"fabia","contents":["bioconda","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bioconductor-fabia","version":"2.56.0","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/fabia.html","license":"LGPL (>= 2.1)","summary":"FABIA: Factor Analysis for Bicluster Acquisition","identifiers":["biotools:fabia"],"description":"Biclustering by \"Factor Analysis for Bicluster Acquisition\" (FABIA). FABIA is a model-based technique for biclustering, that is clustering rows and columns simultaneously. Biclusters are found by factor analysis where both the factors and the loading matrix are sparse. FABIA is a multiplicative model that extracts linear dependencies between samples and feature patterns. It captures realistic non-Gaussian data distributions with heavy tails as observed in gene expression measurements. FABIA utilizes well understood model selection techniques like the EM algorithm and variational approaches and is embedded into a Bayesian framework. FABIA ranks biclusters according to their information content and separates spurious biclusters from true biclusters. The code is written in C.","license_file":"/lib/R/share/licenses/LGPL-3","build":{"number":0,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"],"run_exports":""},"requirements":{"build":[null,"make"],"host":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","r-base","libblas","liblapack","zlib","liblzma-devel"],"run":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","r-base"]},"source_url":["https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/fabia_2.56.0.tar.gz","https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/Archive/fabia/fabia_2.56.0.tar.gz","https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/fabia_2.56.0.tar.gz","https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-fabia/bioconductor-fabia_2.56.0_src_all.tar.gz"],"test":{"commands":["$R -e \"library('fabia')\""]},"parent_recipe":{"name":"bioconductor-fabia","path":"recipes/bioconductor-fabia","version":"2.26.0"}},"biotools":{"id":"fabia","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/fabia","license":"LGPL-2.1-or-later","summary":"Biclustering by \"Factor Analysis for Bicluster Acquisition\" (FABIA). FABIA is a model-based technique for biclustering, that is clustering rows and columns simultaneously. Biclusters are found by factor analysis where both the factors and the loading matrix are sparse. FABIA is a multiplicative model that extracts linear dependencies between samples and feature patterns. It captures realistic non-Gaussian data distributions with heavy tails as observed in gene expression measurements. FABIA utilizes well understood model selection techniques like the EM algorithm and variational approaches and is embedded into a Bayesian framework. FABIA ranks biclusters according to their information content and separates spurious biclusters from true biclusters. The code is written in C.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:00:38Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:13:29.502324Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["2.58.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:fabia","credit":[{"name":"Sepp Hochreiter"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/fabia"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2495"},{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}]}],"name":"fabia","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[],"topic":[{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:fabia:2.20.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"ope